@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title cecli paradigm — pair-programming specialist (precise, low-token, human-guided)

' covers: defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/bridges/cecli.tsv
'
' ── THE LOCAL MODEL GOES THROUGH OLLAMA'S OPENAI-COMPATIBLE API ────────────
' A local model reaches litellm through Ollama's /v1 route, NOT its native one,
' because both litellm ollama providers are broken in this image:
'
'   ollama_chat/<model>   loses its api_base — every call dies with
'                         "Request URL is missing an 'http://' or 'https://'
'                         protocol"
'   ollama/<model>        raises FileNotFoundError
'
' Ollama also serves /v1 and that route works, so the model is spelled
' "openai/<model>" and pointed at it. All three slots take it: CECLI_MODEL,
' CECLI_EDITOR_MODEL and CECLI_WEAK_MODEL.
'
' OPENAI_API_BASE is litellm's name for the endpoint (OPENAI_BASE_URL is the
' SDK's), so that is the variable set. Precedence: whatever `proveo run
' --local-model` already exported wins; otherwise it is derived from
' OLLAMA_API_BASE, defaulting to http://ollama:11434 so a hand-run container
' still works. A "/v1" suffix is appended when absent. OPENAI_API_KEY defaults
' to the literal "ollama", which is what that endpoint expects.
'
' NOTE: this supersedes the older "the ollama_chat/ prefix matters" reading.
' The bridge table may still normalise an id to an ollama prefix
' (_spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml); this block overrides
' the three CECLI_* slots afterwards when PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL is set.
'
' ── THE UI PASSTHROUGHS, AND THE ARGV RULE ─────────────────────────────────
' DARK_MODE (true/1/yes, any case) sets both CECLI_DARK_MODE and
' AIDER_DARK_MODE; CODE_THEME sets CECLI_CODE_THEME. Both fill an empty slot
' only, so an explicit CECLI_* value always wins.
'
' CECLI_AGENT_CONFIG is defaulted only when neither the environment nor a
' project config declares `agent-config:`. Its subagent_paths names
' "$CECLI_HOME/agents" AND "/app/.cecli/agents", which is why proveo_seed
' composes into CECLI_HOME rather than the agent home — see
' _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml.
'
' Evidence and --rules flags are ours to add, and both belong ONLY on a cecli
' invocation. So the argv rule has three cases: no arguments, or a leading
' flag, or a first word that is not one of the passthrough commands
' (cecli, bash, sh, python, python3, node, npm, pnpm, git, curl) — those get
' the flags prepended; a passthrough is exec'd untouched.
'
actor "Developer\nsupplies exact references" as DEV

node "cecli container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "cecli (aider fork, Python/litellm)" as CLI <<app>>
  folder "seeded subagents\n$CECLI_HOME/agents" as SUB <<app>>
  component "Serena MCP (pinned in the image)\ncode intelligence (no native LSP)" as MCP <<app>>
  database "/app — repo (rw)\n.git root ro · /app/output rw" as WS <<db>>
  artifact "CONVENTIONS.md" as CONV <<db>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI : named files + functions
EP ARROW_MAIN CLI : " ""CECLI_MODEL"" · ""CECLI_EDITOR_MODEL"" \n""CECLI_WEAK_MODEL"" (+ AIDER_* aliases) "
EP ARROW_MAIN SUB : seed missing only\n(""CECLI_RESEED=1"" forces)
EP ARROW_OPTIONAL MCP : wire when the ""initialize""\nhandshake ANSWERS
EP ARROW_OPTIONAL CONV : seed when absent
CLI ARROW_MAIN WS : small, deliberate edits
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL SUB : adversarial review · debugging · spec review

note right of CLI
  **Working mode.** Prefer reading named files and
  functions over broad inference; keep token consumption
  minimal; favor small deliberate edits. The agent does
  not autonomously explore the whole repo — the human
  supplies the references.

  **Posture:** conservative. No blanket dangerous flag;
  ""skip_cli_confirmations"" stays false.
end note

note bottom of EP
  Shared entrypoint contract (see
  _spec/packages/lib/steps.puml and
  _spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml):
  non-root any-uid, in-shell ""load_env"" + model bridge,
  git identity bridge + context report, verification
  command discovery, smoke-test mode.

  cecli resolves commit identity through
  ""git config --get"", so the config-env bridge is what
  stops it seeding placeholder identity into the repo.
end note

note bottom of WS
  ""gitMode: ro"" — the root ""\.git"" is mounted read-only in
  the monorepo-subdir case; project state stays under
  ""/app/.cecli"" while home config persists in
  ""~/.proveo/.cecli"".
end note
note bottom of MCP
  **Deleted once, and this is what it lacked.**
  ""command -v serena"" proved a LAUNCHER existed; a
  version skew left the server dead on every boot
  for weeks. Now: pinned by ""SERENA_VERSION"", and
  ""configure_cecli_mcp"" declares nothing unanswered.
end note

note bottom of CONV
  **cecli auto-loads no conventions file at all.** ""CONVENTIONS\.md"" is a
  naming habit rather than a feature, and ""AGENTS\.md"" is not read either —
  both have to be passed with ""--rules"", so the entrypoint hands it
  whichever the project actually ships.
end note

note bottom of CLI
  **Evidence: ""-v"" narrates each step and ""--show-diffs"" prints the patch at
  commit time** — the one place cecli otherwise commits work without
  showing it. ""--show-repo-map"" and ""--show-prompts"" look like they belong
  in the same list but they print and **exit**, so they can never be
  defaults.

  **Local model: cecli reaches Ollama through litellm** — but NEITHER litellm
  ollama provider works in this image, so the route is the OpenAI-compatible
  one. See the header block above for the two failure modes and the spelling
  that replaced them.
end note


@enduml
